  "reasoning": "The patient reports stiffness and weakness in the neck muscles, swollen joints ('joints have grown'), and extreme discomfort when walking. These symptoms point directly to joint inflammation and degeneration. While cervical spondylosis can cause neck stiffness and muscle weakness, it does not explain the swollen joints or the severe walking difficulty caused by joint stiffness. Arthritis comprehensively accounts for all the clinical features described—joint swelling, stiffness, and painful mobility—making it the definitive diagnosis.",
